WEBVTT

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:30.590
Excuse me...

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:38.150
I'm sorry. I often see you here, so I just...

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.510
My father is buried here.

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:47.900
Sorry to be rude, but may I ask your name?

00:00:56.620 --> 00:01:00.120
You must have lost someone very dear to you.

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:05.150
Excuse-

00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:06.490
Come on, we're ready to leave.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:09.840
We have to mail all the invitations out today.

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:08.470
The Flavor of Orsini

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:11.120
This mysterious restaurant is on a road just a little ways from the center of Rome.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:16.060
Buonasera.

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:17.750
We've been expecting you.

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:20.720
He's here!

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:25.010
Mr. Rizzo, a regular, promised to bring him here!

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:33.050
Senator Fassone...

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:36.720
He... He's gorgeous!

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:41.780
<i>Sheesh. Just when I was starting to think better of her, she acts like that?</i>

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:45.070
It sure is nice to see the Madam in good spirits.

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:46.170
If you say so.

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:47.910
Oh, Nicoletta.

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:51.620
The owner is in the back. Take this to him.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:52.580
S-Sure.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:58.130
<i>I still don't get her obsession with gentlemen.</i>

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:00.580
Here you go.

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:04.300
Thank you.

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:05.610
You used to the place yet?

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:07.480
Yes, definitely.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:13.960
<i>The owner really does look so kind...</i>

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:15.900
<i>"Why Olga of all people?"</i>

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:18.650
<i>...et cetera, is what I'd like to ask him.</i>

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:35.620
<i>Come to think of it, I've never really talked to Gigi either.</i>

00:04:37.970 --> 00:04:40.950
<i>But I don't think he dislikes me or anything...</i>

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:44.670
<i>He tipped me off on how to sneak in free dolces...</i>

00:04:46.810 --> 00:04:49.020
<i>What a peculiar man.</i>

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:51.550
<i>I can't get a read on him.</i>

00:04:58.110 --> 00:05:01.410
I heard he was born in the north.

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:03.940
Mr. Fassone must be tired from working in the Senate.

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:05.540
So how about...

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:09.800
Can't we give him something, on the house, to let him relax?

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:18.990
A Piemonte red.

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:21.090
I picked it up on my last day off.

00:05:21.740 --> 00:05:24.280
It'll go very well with his primo course.

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:27.900
That's the one! I knew you'd come through!

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:37.560
You just keep doing whatever you want, don't you?

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:40.470
Some might call that abuse of power.

00:05:40.470 --> 00:05:41.980
Whatever do you mean?

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:45.820
No matter how much you like bespectacled men, that's just playing favorites!

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:48.750
It's not playing favorites!

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:54.850
As the proprietress of this establishment, it's my duty to see that our customers are satisfied.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:56.860
And also...

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:00.620
Follow me.

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:19.480
See? Gigi's a real pro.

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:25.600
Without you saying a word, he'll pick the exact wine that you're craving.

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:43.940
Nicoletta, when you're done with that, bring the owner's dishes back here.

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:45.120
His next course is about ready.

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:45.910
OK.

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:53.200
<i>He comes to refill his glass even though he can't see him drinking it.</i>

00:06:55.550 --> 00:06:58.640
He knows the pace I normally drink at.

00:06:59.090 --> 00:07:01.750
Have you known Gigi a long time?

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:04.610
If I recall, he's been here since the start...

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:07.520
Yeah. Look at the second picture from the right.

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:14.270
That was taken twenty-seven years ago.

00:07:14.270 --> 00:07:15.410
You're so young!

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:20.270
That was taken when my brother and I opened the ristorante next to the winery.

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:22.690
The precursor to this place.

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:25.270
What?!

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:28.650
I manage a winery.

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:31.560
I-I knew that.

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:34.040
The two of you are brothers?

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:35.230
Yeah.

00:07:35.230 --> 00:07:36.150
Half-brothers.

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:40.590
Oh... No wonder you've known each other so long.

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:42.300
Exactly.

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:47.510
But we met when I was twenty-three.

00:07:49.210 --> 00:07:52.400
Yes, I remember it well.

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:56.810
A wine connoisseur that I knew introduced us.

00:07:56.810 --> 00:07:59.570
I was visiting a home in the suburbs of Turin.

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:03.810
Gian Luigi Orsini...

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:05.090
Huh?

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:10.500
My big brother?

00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:16.620
Right. My father told me about you.

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:19.020
Nice to meet you, big bro.

00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:29.910
What are you running off for?

00:08:29.910 --> 00:08:31.010
Did I do something?

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:35.680
My father says we aren't to meet.

00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:45.780
Wait. You're brothers, but you weren't allowed to meet?

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:49.800
Gigi and I share the same mother.

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:53.650
My father managed a winery outside of Rome.

00:08:54.070 --> 00:08:58.290
Gigi's father was a successful businessman in his hometown of Turin.

00:08:58.750 --> 00:09:04.550
So, I was born here and Gigi was born over here.

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:06.340
I see...

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:08.820
But that's not all.

00:09:09.350 --> 00:09:12.020
These two are actually brothers, you see.

00:09:12.420 --> 00:09:17.560
So to me, he's both my half-older brother and my cousin.

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:20.770
So you mean...

00:09:20.770 --> 00:09:25.690
Exactly. My father slept with his older brother's wife.

00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:28.510
And then, I was born.

00:09:40.110 --> 00:09:41.860
It's surprising.

00:09:41.860 --> 00:09:45.470
I didn't expect you to have such an interest in politics.

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:48.980
Of course, you are a talented lawyer,

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:51.800
so I suppose I shouldn't have assumed otherwise.

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:53.990
Table four is asking for the check.

00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:55.460
Oh, sure thing.

00:09:58.300 --> 00:10:00.630
What a fascinating restaurant,

00:10:00.630 --> 00:10:02.820
staffed by nothing but men in spectacles!

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:08.480
This was actually a gift the owner made to his beloved wife.

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:13.840
Yes, I'm blessed to have met such a wonderful husband.

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:14.810
Indeed.

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:18.640
Thank you.

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:26.620
Umm, so Gigi and your mother, she...

00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:28.890
Yes, she passed away.

00:10:28.890 --> 00:10:32.240
Well before Gigi and I ever met her.

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:38.690
My uncle never forgave my father for what he did.

00:10:38.690 --> 00:10:43.760
He said that by sleeping with his own brother's wife, he severed all familial ties.

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:47.760
He cut all ties with me, that stupid older brother of mine.

00:10:50.970 --> 00:10:53.540
But it's all true.

00:10:56.170 --> 00:11:00.530
Seems he's a sommelier. That's what was on his business card.

00:11:00.530 --> 00:11:03.780
Gigi, really? I see.

00:11:04.370 --> 00:11:08.370
I'm going to stop by the restaurant where he works, Dad.

00:11:10.650 --> 00:11:13.530
Then, I have a favor to ask you.

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:26.220
Hey there, big bro.

00:11:28.350 --> 00:11:30.180
My dad had a message for you.

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:32.930
"Stop by anytime for a drink."

00:11:40.230 --> 00:11:42.220
Look how you've grown.

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:46.900
Seems he took a liking to our winery.

00:11:46.900 --> 00:11:49.350
He soon started coming there alone.

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:52.860
He was a real character, back then.

00:11:53.640 --> 00:11:56.520
I started to like him myself.

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:00.830
What a waste.

00:12:01.910 --> 00:12:06.980
I had a brother like you all these years, and yet we spent them apart.

00:12:08.010 --> 00:12:10.630
I wish I had met you earlier.

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:27.450
We're not involved in our fathers' feud,

00:12:27.770 --> 00:12:30.560
so let's stay on good terms, Gigi.

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:49.760
My father and I talked the other day.

00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:54.670
We tossed around the idea of opening a fun, little ristorante next door,

00:12:54.670 --> 00:12:57.220
to go along with the wine we're making.

00:12:58.030 --> 00:13:01.270
If you'd be willing, I could use your help,

00:13:01.270 --> 00:13:03.540
in making the wine list.

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:05.250
This is an outrage!

00:13:06.920 --> 00:13:12.100
I made it very clear that you were not to meet with people from that household!

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:15.930
Don't you dare get near him ever again!

00:13:15.930 --> 00:13:16.630
Dad.

00:13:16.630 --> 00:13:17.420
What?!

00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:22.280
I've made up my mind to work in the ristorante that Lorenzo is opening.

00:13:23.180 --> 00:13:24.660
Over my dead body!

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:26.530
I've made up my mind.

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:30.970
You may have your feud, but it's got nothing to do with us.

00:13:30.970 --> 00:13:33.680
The only wine we drink is from Piemonte!

00:13:33.680 --> 00:13:35.950
Lorenzo's wines are just as good.

00:13:35.950 --> 00:13:36.960
Gigi!

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:52.660
Apparently, my uncle always had a weak heart.

00:13:54.210 --> 00:13:57.510
Gigi asked their servant to confirm that he's dead,

00:13:57.510 --> 00:13:59.530
and then called the police.

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:03.790
I... killed my father.

00:14:11.180 --> 00:14:12.650
Well, yeah...

00:14:12.650 --> 00:14:15.590
Hearing the circumstances, it sounds like an accident.

00:14:15.590 --> 00:14:18.280
But we still need to ask him if he killed him.

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:24.980
So I figured we'll let him spend the night in jail, then take him home tomorrow.

00:14:40.890 --> 00:14:45.870
And then, we opened the ristorante a year later.

00:14:47.390 --> 00:14:49.160
Those were some times.

00:14:51.890 --> 00:14:53.120
Pardon me.

00:14:53.880 --> 00:14:55.080
It's lasagna.

00:14:55.340 --> 00:14:56.170
Thanks.

00:14:57.280 --> 00:15:00.480
Teo commented that you've been gone a while.

00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:02.140
Please excuse me.

00:15:02.430 --> 00:15:03.090
Sure.

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:06.270
Was he telling you about Gigi?

00:15:06.270 --> 00:15:08.890
Yes. I'm so surprised.

00:15:08.890 --> 00:15:11.070
I had no idea he was the owner's brother.

00:15:11.420 --> 00:15:15.590
Gigi does the books every night, too.

00:15:15.590 --> 00:15:20.210
The owner operates the winery too, so he's quite busy.

00:15:20.800 --> 00:15:22.860
Oh, that's why...

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:35.210
He's eating a lot today.

00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:36.510
He eats too much.

00:15:38.530 --> 00:15:42.180
Though, I don't think he does whatever he wants because they're brothers.

00:15:42.180 --> 00:15:45.260
I think he'd be like that no matter where he was.

00:15:45.670 --> 00:15:48.050
The owner's story makes me feel that way.

00:15:48.050 --> 00:15:49.480
I agree.

00:15:50.980 --> 00:15:53.650
Grazie. I'll be back.

00:15:53.650 --> 00:15:54.640
Ciao!

00:15:55.000 --> 00:15:57.730
The Senator seemed satisfied!

00:15:57.730 --> 00:15:59.620
He might come back someday!

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:03.410
It was nothing. I was just doing my job.

00:16:03.410 --> 00:16:06.380
But this might get us some good publicity.

00:16:06.380 --> 00:16:09.510
And not for the spectacles, but for the food.

00:16:09.510 --> 00:16:13.880
No, no... Furio's cooking and Teo's dolces are already well-known in town...

00:16:13.880 --> 00:16:15.620
You don't believe that, do you?

00:16:15.920 --> 00:16:18.130
But anyway, thanks, you guys!

00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:21.180
The food was delicious today, as usual!

00:16:21.180 --> 00:16:24.030
Oh, no. Just the fact you eat it is thanks enough.

00:16:24.520 --> 00:16:29.150
Look, Mommy really wants to get married to someone,

00:16:29.150 --> 00:16:32.250
but he told me he won't get married to someone who's been divorced.

00:16:32.250 --> 00:16:34.250
So you understand, right?

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:39.200
<i>I think I understand why the owner opposes that.</i>

00:16:41.090 --> 00:16:43.010
<i>His parents were like that...</i>

00:16:43.010 --> 00:16:47.490
<i>And two brothers with the same woman... I'd better stop this train of thought.</i>

00:16:47.490 --> 00:16:52.470
<i>He just doesn't want the same thing to happen again.</i>

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:02.400
That label... That bottle's from the owner's winery, isn't it?

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:12.390
For me?

00:17:18.030 --> 00:17:19.210
It's delicious!

00:17:19.210 --> 00:17:23.420
It's an '82. The year the ristorante opened.

00:17:26.780 --> 00:17:29.630
Ma'am, you have a phone call from Mr. Rizzo.

00:17:29.630 --> 00:17:30.730
Oh!

00:17:31.130 --> 00:17:33.920
Grazie! Thanks for tonight!

00:17:33.920 --> 00:17:36.310
Oh, right. I wanted to tell you what happened...

00:17:36.810 --> 00:17:39.430
She sure is a lively one.

00:17:40.710 --> 00:17:42.630
You're her daughter, aren't you?

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:46.480
<i>Claudio wouldn't have told him...</i>

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:51.430
Why do you say that? We don't look alike at all.

00:17:52.970 --> 00:17:54.450
You share the same smile.

00:18:00.990 --> 00:18:03.130
Yeah! Exactly!

00:18:04.780 --> 00:18:07.500
OK, I'll be waiting for you.

00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:08.650
Ciao!

00:18:36.290 --> 00:18:40.070
<i>He knows what wine people want to drink because he observes them closely.</i>

00:18:46.160 --> 00:18:48.910
<i>Two brothers going after the same woman...</i>

00:18:49.380 --> 00:18:52.170
<i>Love takes all shapes and sizes, I guess.</i>

00:18:56.260 --> 00:18:57.390
Buonasera.

00:18:57.690 --> 00:18:58.720
Buonasera.

00:19:00.260 --> 00:19:03.440
Hey, the Senator stopped by, didn't he?

00:19:03.440 --> 00:19:05.340
How did Olga react?

00:19:05.340 --> 00:19:06.820
You know an awful lot, don't you?

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:12.310
She couldn't stop talking about it back in the office. It was nuts.

00:19:12.310 --> 00:19:15.060
Gabrielle? You're late!

00:19:15.390 --> 00:19:16.920
What were you doing all night?

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:18.380
Come on, sit down!

00:19:18.380 --> 00:19:22.020
So yeah, the Senator just left a little while ago,

00:19:22.020 --> 00:19:24.800
but he was drop-dead gorgeous!

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:46.260
Congratulations!

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:49.830
I hope you have a happy marriage!

00:19:49.830 --> 00:19:51.110
Congratulations!

00:19:57.320 --> 00:20:02.450
Hi. I'm sorry about the other day.

00:20:02.870 --> 00:20:05.430
We're going to live together in Palermo.

00:20:06.040 --> 00:20:11.250
So, I don't think you'll see me there very often.

00:20:11.650 --> 00:20:13.220
How does she know this man?

00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:18.920
I see him quite a bit. Whenever we're visiting the cemetery.

00:20:20.050 --> 00:20:23.070
I don't want my father to be lonely,

00:20:23.460 --> 00:20:27.520
but am I being a bad daughter for moving so far away?

00:20:27.860 --> 00:20:29.470
Not at all.

00:20:30.430 --> 00:20:32.210
I'm sure he's happy for you,

00:20:33.260 --> 00:20:34.720
up in heaven.

00:20:41.860 --> 00:20:43.250
Thank you.

00:20:43.590 --> 00:20:47.470
I wish a life of eternal happiness for you as well.

00:20:59.770 --> 00:21:15.980
A Husband and Wife

00:21:00.610 --> 00:21:02.950
I should be able to have fun, too.

00:21:03.510 --> 00:21:07.090
The girls know what kind of guy I am,

00:21:07.090 --> 00:21:09.970
so only the ones looking for a good time approach me.

00:21:09.970 --> 00:21:14.470
When those women weren't around, I was completely alone.

00:21:14.470 --> 00:21:15.970
But now, I...

00:22:54.940 --> 00:22:58.560
But now, I... won't miss the next episode!
